    "https://phh.tbe.taleo.net/phh02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=WILMU&cws=60&rid=1355": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Employment Opportunities Adjunct Faculty Positions Full-Time Faculty and Staff Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applicant Resources New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Instructor - Doctor of Nursing Practice - Project Courses Location Online Learning Job Code 1355 Apply Now College of Health Professions and Natural Sciences Adjunct Faculty for Doctor of Nursing Practice Program http://www.wilmu.edu/health/dnp_about.aspx Nurses in advanced practice roles need to have forward-thinking clinical expertise and leadership skills at their command to promote the application and implementation of evidence-based practices linked to original scientific research. Accomplishing this goal requires linking health policy, informatics, population health, and business practices to the care of individuals, families, and communities. The Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) at Wilmington University is a terminal degree designed to prepare advanced nurses to meet the nation's increasingly complex health care need. The Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) program is seeking adjunct faculty to teach the DNP Project Courses. Courses are offered online and, in a weekend intensive format. A minimum of 2 virtual synchronous sessions are required for each online course. One weekend in-person or via Zoom is required for the weekend-intensive format. https://www.wilmu.edu/courses/coursedescriptions.aspx?subcode=DNP Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing or related field (Master’s Degree in Nursing is required if the doctoral degree is not in nursing) Demonstrated expertise in evidenced based practice At least 5 years of clinical/practical experience At least 3 years of teaching experience at the doctoral level Experience advising doctoral student project development and implementation Preferred Qualifications: Unencumbered licensure as a Registered Nurse (RN), if applicable. National Board Certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN), if applicable. At least 1 publication (either a QI project or original research study) in a peer-reviewed journal within the last 5 years. Understanding of the AACN Essentials. Understanding of the AONL Nurse Executive Competencies. Additional Requirements: Understand and comply with the mission and values of Wilmington University. Proficient computer skills and the ability to use MS Office software. Experience using Canvas or other Learning Management System. Willingness to complete Wilmington University’s Learning Management System training. Ability to abide by tight deadlines required of a 7-week block or 15-week semester format curriculum. Knowledge of various instructional strategies designed to meet the course objectives and enhance student learning. Ability to develop a personalized course outline designed to follow a course template provided by the University. Ability to provide relevant field/work experience to the instructional content of the course. Interested applicants must complete the application, and attach resume including a cover letter indicating interest and any other relevant information not included in your resume. Include a copy of your transcripts for the highest degree earned. Limited Benefits:  Tuition (after eligibility is met), 403(b) Employee Participation Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phh.tbe.taleo.net/phh02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=WILMU&cws=60&rid=1284": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Employment Opportunities Adjunct Faculty Positions Full-Time Faculty and Staff Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applicant Resources New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Instructor - Healthcare Economics and Business of Practice Location Multiple Job Code 1284 Apply Now College of Health Professions and Natural Sciences Adjunct Faculty – Doctor of Nursing Practice Program– Online and Weekend Intensive Formats http://www.wilmu.edu/health/dnp_about.aspx Nurses in advanced practice roles need to have forward-thinking clinical expertise and leadership skills at their command to promote the application and implementation of evidence-based practices linked to original scientific research. Accomplishing this goal requires linking health policy, informatics, population health, and business practices to the care of individuals, families, and communities. The Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) at Wilmington University is a terminal degree designed to prepare advanced nurses to meet the nation's increasingly complex health care needs. The Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) program is currently accepting applications for adjunct faculty to teach DNP 7105: Healthcare Economics and the Business of Practice. Courses are offered online and, in a weekend intensive format. A minimum of 2 virtual synchronous sessions are required for each online course. One weekend in-person or via Zoom is required for the weekend-intensive format.  A course description is available at DNP7105 Course Description . Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing or related field, i.e. DNP, PhD, EdD, DHSc, DrPH, DBA. Demonstrated expertise in healthcare economics and financial structures. At least 5 years of experience working as a leader in healthcare finance. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching at the graduate or doctroral level Unencumbered licensure as a Registered Nurse (RN), if applicable. National Board Certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN), if applicable. At least 1 publication (either a QI project or original research study) in a peer-reviewed journal within the last 5 years At least 1 publication (either a QI project or original research study) in a peer-reviewed journal within the last 5 years. Understanding of the AACN Essentials. Understanding of the AONE Nurse Executive Competencies. Additional Requirements: Understand and comply with the mission and values of Wilmington University. Submit a teaching philosophy teaching sample following these guidelines: provide a description of your teaching philosophy. Your description should be no more than 1.5 pages in length and should include the following information: (1) A brief statement (5-7 sentences) explaining how you plan to provide excellence in teaching, relevancy of curriculum, and individual attention to students, which is the cornerstone of Wilmington University’s mission statement. (2) Based on your statement above, please briefly answer the following questions: (a) Explain your beliefs, theories and/or methods regarding teaching and how they shape your concept of successful teaching? (b) How do you know when you are teaching effectively? (c) How do you develop and maintain positive relationships with students? (d) How do you create a supportive learning environment? and (3) Include a summary of your thoughts on education and the role that you feel you could play in developing students to be successful in their discipline, career, and life. (This statement can be pasted in the area provided in the application or attached via the attachments area of the application.) Proficient computer skills and be able to use MS Office software. Experience in using Canvas technology or other Learning Management System. Be willing to complete Wilmington University’s Learning Management System training. Be able to abide by tight deadlines required of a 7-week block or 15-week semester format curriculum. Knowledge of various instructional strategies designed to meet the course instructional objectives and add to student learning. Able to develop a personalized course outline designed to follow a generic syllabus provided by the University. Able to provide relevant work experience to the instructional content of the course. Complete the application, attach your resume, include a cover letter indicating any other relevant information not included in your application or resume, and a copy of your transcripts for the highest degree earned. Limited Benefits:  Tuition (after eligibility is met), 403(b) Employee Participation Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phh.tbe.taleo.net/phh02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=WILMU&cws=60&rid=1719": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Employment Opportunities Adjunct Faculty Positions Full-Time Faculty and Staff Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applicant Resources New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Instructor Pool: Business, Leadership, and Organizational Management Topics Location Multiple Job Code 1719 Apply Now EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY POSITION: Adjunct Instructor Pool – Business, Leadership, and Organizational Management Topics. Summary: The College of Professional and Continuing Education at Wilmington University seeks experienced professionals to join a facilitator pool for a growing portfolio of workforce and leadership development programs. The University is seeking engaging practitioners, trainers, consultants, coaches, managers, and executives who can deliver highly interactive professional development experiences for adult learners. About the College of Professional and Continuing Education. The College of Professional and Continuing Education provides workforce-focused learning opportunities that help individuals develop new skills, earn credentials, advance their careers, and meet the evolving needs of employers and communities. Learn more about us at wilmu.edu/continuinged. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and professional experience. Demonstrated expertise in one or more professional development topic areas. Experience teaching, training, facilitating, coaching, consulting, or leading teams. Strong presentation and interpersonal communication skills. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Leadership and management Change management Performance management Organizational development Conflict resolution Negotiation and persuasion Critical thinking and decision-making Team effectiveness and collaboration Communication and influence Human resources and talent development Project and operations leadership Artificial intelligence and the future of work Business strategy and organizational effectiveness Preferred Qualifications Master's degree or advanced professional credentials. Experience facilitating adult learning in corporate, nonprofit, healthcare, education, or government environments. Industry certifications relevant to area of expertise (e.g., SHRM, HRCI, Prosci, PMP, ICF, CPTD, Lean, Six Sigma, AI-related credentials, etc.). Experience delivering workshops, leadership development programs, or workforce training initiatives. Responsibilities Facilitate engaging, learner-centered professional development programs. Lead discussions, activities, case studies, simulations, and applied learning experiences. Connect concepts to real-world workplace challenges. Encourage participation, reflection, and knowledge sharing among adult learners. Support a positive, inclusive, and high-quality learning experience. Maintain professionalism and represent Wilmington University effectively in interactions with participants and organizational partners. Hours of Employment . Applicants should have the flexibility to deliver programming during the day and the ability to deliver programming in person at one of Wilmington University’s campuses. Compensation . Compensation varies by assignment and is determined based on factors such as program length, content area expertise, professional credentials, facilitation experience, and the level of preparation and instructional responsibility required. Application Process . Interested applicants should complete the application, attach your resume or CV, and a cover letter detailing information you did not include in your resume or application. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phh.tbe.taleo.net/phh02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=WILMU&cws=60&rid=1721": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Employment Opportunities Adjunct Faculty Positions Full-Time Faculty and Staff Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applicant Resources New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Instructor Pool – AI in the Workplace Location Multiple Job Code 1721 Apply Now EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY POSITION: Adjunct Instructor Pool – AI in the Workplace Summary: The College of Professional and Continuing Education at Wilmington University seeks experienced professionals to join a roster of facilitators for various AI in the Workplace programs. These programs are designed to help professionals understand how artificial intelligence is transforming the workplace and to develop practical skills for using AI tools responsibly, effectively, and ethically. Facilitators will lead engaging learning experiences that help participants apply AI concepts and technologies to real-world workplace challenges. Current and future offerings may range from introductory AI literacy workshops to topic-specific courses focused on AI applications, productivity, innovation, and organizational transformation. Facilitators will serve as subject matter experts who develop curriculum, facilitate adult learning environments, enrich participant learning through professional experience and practical examples, and help learners confidently navigate the rapidly evolving AI landscape. About the College of Professional and Continuing Education. The College of Professional and Continuing Education provides workforce-focused learning opportunities that help individuals develop new skills, earn credentials, advance their careers, and meet the evolving needs of employers and communities. Learn more about us at wilmu.edu/continuinged. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and professional experience in a relevant field. Demonstrated knowledge of generative AI tools and applications. Professional experience using AI technologies in business, education, healthcare, government, technology, or another industry setting. Experience teaching, training, facilitating, coaching, consulting, or leading teams. Strong communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills. Ability to engage adult learners through interactive instruction. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Generative AI applications and tools AI literacy and workforce readiness Prompt engineering AI productivity and workflow optimization AI for business operations AI for leadership and management AI strategy and implementation Responsible and ethical AI use AI governance and risk management Data-informed decision making AI in education, healthcare, government, or business Digital transformation and innovation Emerging technologies and the future of work Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in a relevant discipline. Experience designing or delivering AI-related training programs. Professional experience leading technology adoption, innovation initiatives, or digital transformation efforts. Experience delivering both in-person and virtual instruction. Industry certifications related to artificial intelligence, data analytics, technology, project management, or professional development. Experience working with diverse adult learner populations. Strongly Preferred Qualifications. Applicants with these qualifications will be considered first. Significant experience applying AI tools in professional environments. A demonstrated ability to translate complex technical concepts into practical applications for non-technical audiences. Experience facilitating executive education, workforce development, or organizational training programs. Expertise in responsible AI, AI governance, or organizational AI adoption. Recognized professional accomplishments related to artificial intelligence, innovation, or digital transformation. Responsibilities Facilitate engaging, learner-centered AI and workforce development programs. Develop curriculum and instructional materials. Demonstrate AI tools, techniques, and real-world applications. Lead discussions, activities, simulations, and hands-on learning experiences. Help learners understand both the opportunities and limitations of AI technologies. Connect AI concepts to workplace challenges, organizational goals, and industry-specific use cases. Foster an inclusive and interactive learning environment. Adapt examples and discussions to meet the needs of diverse audiences. Collaborate with program staff to support continuous improvement and participant success. Maintain current knowledge of developments in artificial intelligence and related technologies. Hours of Employment . Applicants should have the flexibility to deliver programming during the day and the ability to deliver programming in person at one of Wilmington University’s campuses. Compensation . Compensation varies by assignment and is determined based on factors such as course length, subject matter expertise, professional credentials, facilitation experience, and other requirements associated with the successful delivery of the program. Application Process . Interested applicants should complete the application, attach your resume or CV, and a cover letter including a brief statement describing relevant AI, technology, and facilitation experience, a summary of AI-related expertise and preferred instructional topics, and provide examples of AI tools, projects, or initiatives utilized professionally. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phh.tbe.taleo.net/phh02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=WILMU&cws=60&rid=1720": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Employment Opportunities Adjunct Faculty Positions Full-Time Faculty and Staff Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applicant Resources New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Pool: Early Childhood Education CDA Certification Location Multiple Job Code 1720 Apply Now EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY POSITION: Adjunct Instructor Pool – Early Childhood Education CDA Certification Summary: The College of Professional and Continuing Education at Wilmington University is seeking qualified facilitators to lead Child Development Associate (CDA) credential preparation courses. These courses support current and aspiring early childhood educators as they develop the competencies, knowledge, and professional portfolio required to earn the nationally recognized CDA credential. We are seeking experienced professionals who are passionate about early childhood education, adult learning, and helping learners achieve meaningful professional goals. Facilitators will serve as subject matter experts who deliver CDA aligned curriculum, enrich learning through professional experience and practical examples, and support learners throughout their CDA preparation journey. About the College of Professional and Continuing Education. The College of Professional and Continuing Education provides workforce-focused learning opportunities that help individuals develop new skills, earn credentials, advance their careers, and meet the evolving needs of employers and communities. Learn more about us at wilmu.edu/continuinged. Required Qualifications Associate's degree or higher in Early Childhood Education, Child Development, Education, Human Services, or a related field. Professional experience working in early childhood education settings. Knowledge of child development principles and best practices in early childhood education. Experience teaching, training, coaching, mentoring, or facilitating learning for adults. Strong communication, interpersonal, and technology skills, including the ability to facilitate online instruction. Preferred Qualifications Current or former Child Development Associate (CDA) credential holder. Bachelor's degree or higher in Early Childhood Education or a related field. Experience supporting individuals pursuing the CDA credential. Experience delivering online or hybrid instruction. Familiarity with CDA competency standards, professional portfolio requirements, and the CDA assessment process. Responsibilities Facilitate engaging online learning experiences for adult learners pursuing the CDA credential. Lead weekly synchronous online class sessions. Deliver CDA aligned curriculum and instructional materials. Foster a supportive, inclusive, and learner-centered classroom environment. Connect course concepts to authentic early childhood education practices and real-world scenarios. Provide feedback, coaching, and guidance to learners throughout the course. Monitor learner progress and encourage successful course completion. Support learners as they prepare professional portfolios and work toward meeting CDA requirements. Collaborate with program staff to maintain a high-quality learning experience. Compensation . Compensation varies by assignment and is determined based on factors such as course length, subject matter expertise, professional credentials, facilitation experience, and other requirements associated with the successful delivery of the program. Application Process . Interested applicants should complete the application, attach your resume or CV, and a cover letter including a brief statement of relevant early childhood education and instructional experience, including a summary of experience related to CDA preparation, coaching, mentoring, or credential attainment. Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phh.tbe.taleo.net/phh02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=WILMU&cws=60&rid=1694": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Employment Opportunities Adjunct Faculty Positions Full-Time Faculty and Staff Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applicant Resources New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Professor of Law Location Brandywine Site Job Code 1694 Apply Now EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY DATE: April 24, 2026 FROM: Human Resources POSITION: Adjunct Professors of Law The Wilmington University School of Law welcomes applications from experienced lawyers, judges, and law school instructors who are interested in serving as Adjunct Professor of Law. This position is a part-time, non-tenured faculty position. The successful candidate will be expected to achieve and maintain excellence in teaching at the School of Law. The Wilmington University School of Law see broad access to affordable legal education within a student-centered culture. The law school’s goals: (1) hiring faculty chosen for their extensive experience, commitment to excellence in teaching, and dedication to making a difference in the lives of their students; (2) enrolling students who reflect the diverse communities they will serve in Delaware and the national legal community; (3) offering course schedules and curricula that have been crafted to maximize the benefit for students who may be balancing professional and personal commitments in addition to their legal studies; (4) providing an educational program focused on excellence in developing practice-related competencies, through a curriculum mapped to those competencies and using best instructional practices; (5) bridging the gap between theory and practice through in externships that provide hands-on opportunities to help practicing attorneys solve real challenges; and (6) creating opportunity for our students by keeping tuition and debt low and producing graduates with high value and ability in multiple segments of the market for legal services. There are Adjunct Professor openings to teach the following courses in the School of Law for the Fall 2026  and Spring 2027 terms and General Pool: Fall 2026 - Available Courses Spring 2027 - Available Courses Administrative Law C onflict of Laws Bankruptcy Law Employment Law Employment Law Healthcare Law Federal Courts Pretrial Advocacy Skills Legal Writing I Race and the Law Seminar Legislation and Regulations Trial Advocacy Skills Trial Advocacy Skills Indicate on your application and in your cover letter, the course and the term you are interested in teaching. Course descriptions are available on the University's website at https://wilmu.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/school-of-law-catalog/school-of-law-course-descriptions/ . The successful candidate will possess the following required qualifications: J.D. degree from an ABA accredited law school. Admitted to the bar of any state. Strong academic and professional qualifications. Sufficient and high-quality practice experience to be a foundation for teaching in the School of Law's educational program. Commitment to the goals of the School of Law and its curricular and instructional methods and goals. Understand the mission and values of Wilmington University. Possess strong communication skills. Possess excellent computer skills and the ability to use MS Office Software. Possess knowledge of various instruction strategies designed to meet the instructional objectives and add to student learning. Successful candidates must complete the online Wilmington University Teaching and Learning (Expectations and LMS) via the New Faculty Orientation-Parts 1 and 2 after being hired. Responsibilities include (but are not limited to): Teach as needed by Law School administration. Generally, adjuncts will not teach more than 1-3 class sections per academic year. Demonstrate the ability to achieve excellence in teaching and in mentoring students in their professional development. Follow the instructional and curricular practices of the School of Law, including use of the Canvas Learning Management System, learning outcomes, utilizing multiple assessments, and research and writing modules within a course, as appropriate, with support from other faculty as well as research librarians. Hours of Employment: Classes are scheduled Monday – Thursday between the hours of 9:00 am – 9:35 p.m. All faculty should anticipate teaching needs in both the day and evening programs. Interested applicants should include the following in their application. All document should be attached via the \"attachments\" area of the online application form: A resume or CV A cover letter detailing how the experience and education meet the qualifications needed to teach courses in the program.  Adjunct faculty candidates should set forth their availability in their application cover letter. Copies of t ranscripts that show the institution with J.D. degree awarded (unofficial copies are acceptable - do not mail transcripts to Wilmington University. Statement of your teaching philosophy : o Completed writing prompt (Teaching Philosophy): Provide a description of your teaching philosophy. Your description should be no more than 1.5 pages in length and should include the following information: (1) A brief statement (5-7 sentences) explaining how you plan to provide excellence in teaching, a relevant curriculum, and individual attention to students, which is the cornerstone of Wilmington University’s mission statement. (2) Based on your statement above, please briefly answer the following questions: (a) Explain your beliefs, theories and/or methods regarding teaching and how they shape your concept of successful teaching. (b) How do you know when you are teaching effectively? (c) How do you develop and maintain positive relationships with students? (d) How do you create a supportive learning environment? (3) Include a summary of your thoughts on education and the role that you feel you could play in helping students to be successful in their discipline, career, and life. (This statement should be attached via the attachments area of the application, enter attached in the question's field). All documents must be submitted with the application for full consideration. Back Share Apply Now"
    }
  },
